    "title": "pandas.Series.dt.unit — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1661.gf74cda2e6e documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.dt.unit#\n\n- Series.dt.unit[source]#\n- The precision unit of the datetime data. Returns the precision unit for the dtype. It means the smallest time frame that can be stored within this dtype. \n  - Returns:\n    - str\n    - Unit string representation (e.g. “ns”).\n See also \n  - `TimelikeOps.as_unit`\n  - Converts to a specific unit.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.DatetimeIndex([\"2020-01-02 01:02:03.004005006\"]) >>> idx.unit 'ns' >>> idx.as_unit(\"s\").unit 's'",
    "markdown_length": 467,
